{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793209751,"nonce":"PSpattM0SBIVdpHE6vtY0eeFGRc=","title":"Preserve active nested rounded clips beneath larger ancestors","message":"RayDE's Hybrid and Expressive editor cards paint square child backgrounds outside their rounded bottom corners. A nested card with overflow:hidden and the same or a smaller radius than its outer window reproduces this in Ashui's native display list: all four clip radii become zero.\n\nclip_data retains only the largest nominal radius before calculating the intersection. An unrelated outer corner can win that selection, then be discarded because its source corner does not reach the intersection. The active inner corner was already lost.\n\nCompute the bounds intersection first, then consider every source corner that reaches it and keep the strongest remaining radius. Keep the iterator clone allocation-free and preserve existing rectangular, transformed, shadow, canvas and layer clipping behavior.\n\nThe isolated Haxe probe fails on the pinned ABI with [0,0,0,0]. Rust regressions cover equal/larger inactive outer radii, active outer rounding under a sharp child and sharp cuts beyond a rounded corner. Real display-list tests pass after the patch; Ashui GPU pixel coverage and RayDE browser theme checks follow.","files":null}]}